Address <code>https://&lt;your AgentCanvas&gt;/api/v1/deployments/&lt;id&gt;/mcp</code> Transport Streamable HTTP (every answer is one JSON message; no server-sent stream) Sign-in <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;deployment key&gt;</code> Tools one tool named after the workflow, with the workflow's input fields; plus <code>answer</code> when the workflow can pause for a person <p>Claude Desktop connects to remote servers through <code>mcp-remote</code> (needs Node.js). Add this to <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code> and restart Claude Desktop:</p> <pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "my-workflow": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://&lt;your AgentCanvas&gt;/api/v1/deployments/&lt;id&gt;/mcp",
               "--header", "Authorization: Bearer &lt;deployment key&gt;"]
    }
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>Clients that support remote MCP servers with headers (Cursor, VS Code, agent frameworks such as LangChain's MCP adapter or the OpenAI Agents SDK) take the address and the header directly.</p> <p>When a run pauses for an approval or a question, the tool's answer says so and gives a <code>thread_id</code>; the calling agent continues it with <code>answer</code> (<code>approve: true</code> or <code>false</code>, or <code>text</code> for a question). To continue a conversation, pass the <code>thread_id</code> of the earlier run to the workflow's tool.</p>
